---

<section class="relative pt-20 pb-24 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-6">
      Open specification · Public draft v1.1 · CC-BY-4.0
    </p>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-6">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 leading-[1.1]">
          Run your business with AI agents, without getting locked in.
        </h1>

        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          YAIBOS is an open specification for running a business with AI agents. It starts with Base, the system Samuel uses today: company context, skills, role agents, and tools in a second brain you own. Skills give AI reusable instructions for your business procedures (SOPs). Run them through a compatible AI app, or harness, such as Claude Code or Codex. You can change harnesses and keep the same business files.
        </p>

        <p class="text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Base works on its own. The optional Cockpit profile describes a dashboard for launching and following skills; Team adds shared work and permissions. The spec sets out what each profile needs and what you keep if you switch.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-2 text-sm">
          <a
            href="/spec"
            class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-semibold transition-colors">
            Read the spec
          </a>
          <a
            href="/implementations"
            class="px-6 py-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white hover:bg-slate-50 text-slate-800 font-semibold transition-colors">
            See the scorecard
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-2 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-blue-600 live-indicator"></span>
          <span>Weekly tech watch:</span>
          <a href="/newsletter" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
            The Sovereign AI & Harness Radar ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The v1 idea in one picture: vault -> harness -> model -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 space-y-3 text-sm">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 p-4">
            <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Your second brain <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(Markdown + git, you own it)</span></div>
            <pre class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">├── AGENTS.md   company context
├── SOP/        procedures
├── Tools.md    MCP servers, CLIs
└── Areas/      knowledge</pre>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center text-slate-400" aria-hidden="true">↓ synced to</div>
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 p-4">
            <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Compatible harness <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(replaceable)</span></div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, or another harness with a verified adapter.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center text-slate-400" aria-hidden="true">↓ uses</div>
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 p-4">
            <div class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Supported model <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(replaceable)</span></div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Through the chosen harness and each person's official AI plan or API key.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
